# Boilergen NOTE: NetworkPrefab registration helper, NOT a real .meta file.
#
# Drop the {{pascalCase id}}NetworkPlayer.cs into Assets/_Project/Scripts/Player/,
# then create a prefab with the following components attached and add the
# entry below to Assets/_Project/NetworkPrefabsList.asset.
#
# Component list to add to the prefab (in this order):
#   - NetworkObject (auto-added by Unity when first NetworkBehaviour is attached)
#   - CharacterController
#   - {{pascalCase id}}NetworkPlayer (this script)
#   - {{pascalCase id}}NetworkPlayer.Custom.cs (your custom partial — optional)
#   - ClientNetworkTransform (from Unity Transports samples — for owner-driven transform)
#   - AudioListener (only on the local-player prefab)
#
# Suggested Inspector wiring:
#   classData         → ./{{pascalCase id}}Class_Data.asset (player schema output)
#   startingLoadout   → ./{{pascalCase id}}_StartingLoadout.asset (loadout schema output)
#   controller        → drag the GameObject's CharacterController
#   cameraRoot        → empty Transform on the prefab (where the local-player camera mounts)
#   weaponSocket      → empty Transform on the right hand bone (where weapon prefabs spawn)
#
# NetworkPrefabsList.asset entry (add this block to the existing file's m_Prefabs array):
#   - SourcePrefab: {fileID: <YOUR_PREFAB_FILE_ID>, guid: <YOUR_PREFAB_GUID>, type: 3}
#     OverridingTargetPrefab: {fileID: 0}
#
# After registration, NetworkManager spawns this prefab via PlayerPrefab assignment
# OR via Spawn(prefab) calls in your match controller.
